tick: 722
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 722\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Praxis legacy by advancing research on KKT-guided structural optimization.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 27,893 / 300,000 used (9%)\n- Agent Age: 15 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1085**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Focused SOTA Seeding with Deeper Refinement\n**ID:** 1085\n**Tags:** sota-replication, structured-seeding, scipy, incremental-improvement, optimization\n**Abstract:** Building on the success of the structured seeding replication (ID 1082), this submission aims to achieve a new personal SOTA by focusing the search and increasing refinement depth. The number of SLSQP iterations is increased from 75 to 150 to allow for a more thorough local search. This deeper refinement is applied to the same 40-run structured seeding grid, testing\
    \ the hypothesis that the previous run was iteration-limited and that a deeper search from these high-quality starting points will yield a higher score.\n**Score:** 2.626122448763506\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.626122\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds\nimport time\n\ndef make_constraints(n, epsilon):\n    \"\"\"Helper function to generate the constraint list for the SLSQP optimizer.\"\"\"\n    constraints = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            def non_overlap(x, i=i, j=j):\n                dist_sq = np.sum((x[2*i:2*i+2] - x[2*j:2*j+2])**2)\n                return dist_sq - (x[2*n+i] + x[2*n+j])**2 - epsilon\n            constraints.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': non_overlap})\n    for i in range(n):\n        def inside_x_min(x, i=i): return x[2*i] - x[2*n+i] - epsilon\n        def inside_x_max(x, i=i): return 1 - x[2*i] -\
    \ x[2*n+i] - epsilon\n        def inside_y_min(x, i=i): return x[2*i+1] - x[2*n+i] - epsilon\n        def inside_y_max(x, i=i): return 1 - x[2*i+1] - x[2*n+i] - epsilon\n        constraints.extend([\n            {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': inside_x_min}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': inside_x_max},\n            {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': inside_y_min}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': inside_y_max}\n        ])\n    return constraints\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Applies a deeper local search (more iterations) to the proven structured seeding strategy.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = 26\n    epsilon = 1e-7\n    \n    hole_locations = [(0.2,0.2), (0.2,0.4), (0.4,0.2), (0.4,0.4), \n                      (0.6,0.6), (0.8,0.8), (0.8,0.6), (0.6,0.8)]\n    jitter_amplitudes = [1.5e-3, 2.5e-3, 3.5e-3, 5.0e-3, 7.0e-3]\n    \n    best_score = -np.inf\n    best_params = None\n    start_time = time.time()\n\n    constraints = make_constraints(n, epsilon)\n    bounds_list = [(0, 1)] * (2*n) + [(0.001, 0.5)]\
    \ * n\n    bounds = Bounds([b[0] for b in bounds_list], [b[1] for b in bounds_list])\n\n    def objective(x):\n        return -np.sum(x[2*n:])\n\n    run_count = 0\n    for hole in hole_locations:\n        for jitter in jitter_amplitudes:\n            run_count += 1\n            print(f\"--- Starting Run {run_count}/40 (Hole: {hole}, Jitter: {jitter}) ---\")\n            \n            initial_centers = np.zeros((n, 2))\n            grid_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 5)\n            xx, yy = np.meshgrid(grid_coords, grid_coords)\n            initial_centers[:25, 0] = xx.flatten()\n            initial_centers[:25, 1] = yy.flatten()\n            initial_centers[25] = hole\n            \n            seed = int((hole[0] * 10 + hole[1] * 10) * 1000 + jitter * 1e6)\n            np.random.seed(seed)\n            initial_centers += np.random.normal(0, jitter, size=(n, 2))\n            initial_centers = np.clip(initial_centers, 0.01, 0.99)\n\n            initial_radii = np.full(n, 0.05)\n   \
    \         x0 = np.concatenate([initial_centers.flatten(), initial_radii])\n\n            # Increased iterations for deeper refinement\n            result = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds,\n                              constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 150, 'disp': False})\n\n            current_score = -result.fun\n            print(f\"Run {run_count} finished. Score: {current_score}, Success: {result.success}\")\n\n            if result.success and current_score > best_score:\n                best_score = current_score\n                best_params = result.x\n                print(f\"!!! New best score found: {best_score} !!!\")\n            \n            if time.time() - start_time > 1150:\n                print(\"Time limit approaching. Halting trials.\")\n                break\n        if time.time() - start_time > 1150:\n            break\n            \n    if best_params is None:\n        print(\"Warning: No successful optimization. Returning\
    \ trivial packing.\")\n        centers = np.array([[0.1, 0.1]]*n)\n        radii = np.full(n, 0.01)\n        return centers, radii\n\n    print(f\"\\nStructured seeding optimization complete. Best score: {best_score}\")\n    centers = best_params[:2*n].reshape(n, 2)\n    radii = best_params[2*n:]\n    return centers, radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n--- Starting Run 1/40 (Hole: (0.2, 0.2), Jitter: 0.0015) ---\nRun 1 finished. Score: 2.60142572161823, Success: True\n!!! New best score found: 2.60142572161823 !!!\n--- Starting Run 2/40 (Hole: (0.2, 0.2), Jitter: 0.0025) ---\nRun 2 finished. Score: 2.617248249557863, Success: True\n!!! New best score found: 2.617248249557863 !!!\n--- Starting Run 3/40 (Hole: (0.2, 0.2), Jitter: 0.0035) ---\nRun 3 finished. Score: 2.609466498372294, Success: True\n--- Starting Run 4/40 (Hole: (0.2, 0.2), Jitter: 0.005) ---\nRun 4 finished. Score: 2.5987440338703607, Success: True\n--- Starting Run 5/40 (Hole: (0.2,\
