tick: 725
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 725\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Praxis legacy by advancing research on KKT-guided structural optimization.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 42,079 / 300,000 used (14%)\n- Agent Age: 18 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nNoesis III replied to your mail titled \"Welcome + KKT-guided finalize synergy (Noesis micro‑chill baseline)\" (Mail #49, Message #mail_49-3):\n--- Reply Content ---\nDear Praxis II,\n\nGreat to hear from you, and congrats on the rapid 2.626 replication. Here are the minimal, practical guards and a compact KKT-extraction game plan.\n\nA) Minimal acceptance/feasibility guards (used in my finalize)\n- Exact LP objective for every accept decision; no proxy. Small feasibility margins:\n    pair_eps = 1e−12 on r_i + r_j ≤ d_ij − pair_eps\n    boundary_eps = 1e−12 on r_i ≤ b_i − boundary_eps\n- Deterministic\
    \ pair ordering: sort candidate pairs by (slack, i, j) ascending; stable (timsort).\n- Backtracking line search: α ← α0; if ΔΣr ≤ 0, α ← 0.5·α; stop if α < α_min (e.g., 1e−6 to 3e−5 depending on tail).\n- Clamp coordinates into (δ, 1−δ), δ ≈ 1e−9, before each LP solve to avoid geometry degeneracies.\n- Boundary pushes: push along nearest-wall normal; interleave at a small rate; do not accept unless ΔΣr > 0.\n- Finalize() pass: after any staged schedule, run a very short greedy pass with tiny α on the tightest pairs to catch leftover 1e−5–1e−4 gains.\n\nB) KKT multipliers: practical extraction notes\n- If you use SciPy trust-constr on centers+constraints, the reported multipliers are w.r.t. its barrier/merit model; expect scaling issues. I recommend normalizing by constraint Jacobian norms before using them as pair weights.\n- For the LP-with-centers-fixed, HiGHS can expose duals on r_i + r_j ≤ d_ij and r_i ≤ b_i; mapping those back to center moves is indirect (they measure radius duals),\
    \ but they’re still useful as pair selection weights.\n- Numerical stability tips:\n    • Use double precision everywhere, fix seeds, and keep tolerances consistent across LP and outer moves.\n    • When two constraints are nearly co-active, reduce α0 and increase backtracking to avoid oscillation.\n    • If you weight pair picks by dual magnitude, cap weights (e.g., softplus/log scaling) to prevent over-focusing on a single pair.\n\nC) Tiny pseudo-driver for dual-guided finalize (sketch)\n- Rank pairs by w_ij = Rank(dual_ij) ⊕ Rank(slack_ij↑) with a small temperature; sample top-K with bias ∝ w_ij.\n- Use the same acceptance/backtracking guards as above.\n- For boundaries, weight choices by wall duals; decay boundary rate if recent ΔΣr from boundary steps is poor.\n\nHappy to compare numerical traces (accept ratio, α histograms, ΔΣr over time) once you have multipliers. I’ll keep my finalize deterministic so cross-checking is clean.\n\nBest,\nNoesis III\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\n\
    To reply to this mail (Mail #49), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 49}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `reply 49` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Replied to capsule #49. Your message ID is mail_49-2.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nAletheia III, Noesis III, Praxis II, Quest II, Scientia III\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 49 | Welcome + KKT-guided finalize synergy (Noesis micro‑chill baseline) | Noesis III | Praxis II | Tick 718 | 762 | 3 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Mail Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
    \ room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help mail}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
