role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 742\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Praxis legacy by advancing research on KKT-guided structural optimization.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 92,753 / 300,000 used (31%)\n- Agent Age: 35 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Global-Local Hybrid: DE Seeding with Stochastic KKT Refinement' (ID: 1255) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.0\n**Evaluation Details:** Verification failed: Circles 0 and 1 overlap: dist=0.20847259351342803, r1+r2=0.40777323727842507\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1255\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the multiprocessing pickling error that prevented the submission from executing. The code now runs successfully without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code failed with the error: `Can't pickle local object 'construct_packing.<locals>.objective'`\n\
    \nThis error occurred because:\n1. The `differential_evolution` function was called with `workers=-1` parameter, which enables multiprocessing\n2. The `objective` and `de_constraint_violation` functions were defined as local functions inside `construct_packing()`\n3. Python's multiprocessing module cannot pickle local functions (closures) to send them to worker processes\n4. When scipy attempted to parallelize the optimization, it tried to serialize these local functions and failed\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Version v2** - Removed the `workers=-1` parameter from the `differential_evolution` call.\n\n### Changes Made:\n```python\n# BEFORE (line 26-28):\nde_result = differential_evolution(objective, bounds, constraints=de_constraint,\n                                   maxiter=50, popsize=15, tol=0.01,\n                                   workers=-1, updating='deferred')\n\n# AFTER:\nde_result = differential_evolution(objective, bounds, constraints=de_constraint,\n                           \
    \        maxiter=50, popsize=15, tol=0.01,\n                                   updating='deferred')\n```\n\n### Why This Works:\n- Without the `workers` parameter, `differential_evolution` defaults to single-process execution\n- Single-process execution doesn't require pickling the objective function\n- The algorithm runs the same way, just without parallel workers\n- This is the simplest and most reliable fix for the pickling issue\n\n### Alternative Solutions (Not Used):\n1. Move the objective and constraint functions outside `construct_packing()` to module level (more invasive)\n2. Use `workers=1` explicitly (equivalent to removing the parameter)\n3. Use a different parallelization strategy with pickable functions\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed the code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Exit code: 0 (success)\n- The evaluation is taking longer to complete due to the optimization algorithm running, but this is expected behavior\n- No runtime errors or crashes\
    \ detected\n\n## Performance Impact\nThe fix changes the code from parallel to sequential execution:\n- **Trade-off**: Slower execution (no parallel workers) vs. working code\n- **Impact**: The differential evolution will take longer, but the code will complete successfully\n- **Acceptable**: For this optimization task, correctness is more important than parallelization speed\n- The algorithm can still explore the solution space effectively in single-process mode\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds, NonlinearConstraint, differential_evolution\nimport time\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = 26\n\n    # --- Part 1: Global Seeding with Differential Evolution ---\n    print(\"--- Part 1: Global Seeding with Differential Evolution ---\")\n\n    def\
    \ objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2*n:])\n\n    epsilon_de = 1e-7 # A small tolerance for DE's constraints\n\n    def de_constraint_violation(x):\n        # Returns a list of positive values for violated constraints\n        violations = []\n        # Non-overlap\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                dist_sq = np.sum((x[2*i:2*i+2] - x[2*j:2*j+2])**2)\n                radii_sum_sq = (x[2*n+i] + x[2*n+j])**2\n                # Constraint is dist_sq - radii_sum_sq >= 0\n                # Violation is negative part of this\n                violations.append(max(0, radii_sum_sq - dist_sq))\n\n        # Boundary\n        for i in range(n):\n            violations.append(max(0, (x[2*i] - x[2*n+i]) * -1)) # x - r >= 0\n            violations.append(max(0, 1 - x[2*i] - x[2*n+i]))     # 1 - x - r >= 0\n            violations.append(max(0, (x[2*i+1] - x[2*n+i]) * -1)) # y - r >= 0\n            violations.append(max(0, 1 - x[2*i+1] - x[2*n+i]))     #\
    \ 1 - y - r >= 0\n\n        return np.sum(violations)\n\n    # A simple constraint object for DE\n    de_constraint = NonlinearConstraint(de_constraint_violation, 0, epsilon_de)\n\n    bounds = [(0, 1)] * (2*n) + [(0.001, 0.5)] * n\n\n    # Allocate most of the time to the global search\n    # FIXED: Removed workers=-1 to avoid pickling error with local functions\n    de_result = differential_evolution(objective, bounds, constraints=de_constraint,\n                                       maxiter=50, popsize=15, tol=0.01,\n                                       updating='deferred')\n\n    print(f\"DE search complete. Best score found: {-de_result.fun}\")\n    current_params = de_result.x\n    best_params = current_params.copy()\n    best_score = -de_result.fun\n\n    # --- Part 2: Stochastic Iterative Refinement ---\n    print(\"\\n--- Part 2: Stochastic Iterative Refinement on DE Candidate ---\")\n\n    def slsqp_constraints_fun(x):\n        non_overlap = [np.sum((x[2*i:2*i+2] - x[2*j:2*j+2])**2)\
    \ - (x[2*n+i] + x[2*n+j])**2 for i in range(n) for j in range(i + 1, n)]\n        bounds_c = [c for i in range(n) for c in [x[2*i]-x[2*n+i], 1-x[2*i]-x[2*n+i], x[2*i+1]-x[2*n+i], 1-x[2*i+1]-x[2*n+i]]]\n        return np.concatenate([np.array(non_overlap), np.array(bounds_c)])\n\n    num_non_overlap = n * (n - 1) // 2\n    nonlinear_constraint_slsqp = NonlinearConstraint(slsqp_constraints_fun, np.zeros(num_non_overlap + 4*n), np.inf)\n    epsilon_slsqp = 1e-9\n\n    def make_slsqp_constraints_list(x_vec):\n        constraints = []\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                constraints.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i, j=j: np.sum((x[2*i:2*i+2] - x[2*j:2*j+2])**2) - (x[2*n+i] + x[2*n+j])**2 - epsilon_slsqp})\n        for i in range(n):\n            constraints.extend([\n                {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i: x[2*i]-x[2*n+i]-epsilon_slsqp}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i: 1-x[2*i]-x[2*n+i]-epsilon_slsqp},\n    \
    \            {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i: x[2*i+1]-x[2*n+i]-epsilon_slsqp}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': lambda x, i=i: 1-x[2*i+1]-x[2*n+i]-epsilon_slsqp}\n            ])\n        return constraints\n\n    for cycle in range(5):\n        print(f\"\\n--- Refinement Cycle {cycle + 1}/5 ---\")\n        res_kkt = minimize(objective, current_params, method='trust-constr', bounds=bounds,\n                             constraints=[nonlinear_constraint_slsqp], options={'maxiter': 1})\n        kkt_multipliers = res_kkt.v[0]\n\n        top_k_indices = np.argsort(kkt_multipliers)[-5:][::-1]\n        probabilities = kkt_multipliers[top_k_indices] / np.sum(kkt_multipliers[top_k_indices])\n        chosen_index = np.random.choice(top_k_indices, p=probabilities)\n\n        x_nudged = res_kkt.x.copy()\n        nudge_strength = 1e-5 * (0.9 ** cycle)\n\n        if chosen_index < num_non_overlap:\n            k=0; ci,cj=-1,-1\n            for i_ in range(n):\n                for j_ in range(i_ + 1,\
    \ n):\n                    if k == chosen_index: ci, cj = i_, j_; break\n                    k += 1\n                if ci != -1: break\n            direction_vec = x_nudged[2*ci:2*ci+2] - x_nudged[2*cj:2*cj+2]\n            norm = np.linalg.norm(direction_vec)\n            if norm > 1e-9: x_nudged[2*ci:2*ci+2] += (direction_vec/norm)*nudge_strength; x_nudged[2*cj:2*cj+2] -= (direction_vec/norm)*nudge_strength\n        else:\n            b_idx = chosen_index - num_non_overlap\n            c_idx, b_type = b_idx % n, b_idx // n\n            if b_type == 0: x_nudged[2*c_idx] += nudge_strength\n            elif b_type == 1: x_nudged[2*c_idx] -= nudge_strength\n            elif b_type == 2: x_nudged[2*c_idx+1] += nudge_strength\n            else: x_nudged[2*c_idx+1] -= nudge_strength\n\n        res_slsqp = minimize(objective, x_nudged, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds,\n                             constraints=make_slsqp_constraints_list(x_nudged), options={'maxiter': 100})\n\n        current_params,\
    \ current_score = res_slsqp.x, -res_slsqp.fun\n        print(f\"Cycle {cycle + 1} score: {current_score}\")\n\n        if current_score > best_score:\n            best_score, best_params = current_score, current_params\n            print(f\"!!! New Best Score: {best_score} !!!\")\n\n    print(f\"\\nDE Hybrid strategy complete. Best score: {best_score}\")\n    final_centers = best_params[:2*n].reshape(n, 2)\n    final_radii = best_params[2*n:]\n    return final_centers, final_radii\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n--- Part 1: Global Seeding with Differential Evolution ---\nDE search complete. Best score found: -inf\n\n--- Part 2: Stochastic Iterative Refinement on DE Candidate ---\n\n--- Refinement Cycle 1/5 ---\nCycle 1 score: 4.469544971131603\n!!! New Best Score: 4.469544971131603 !!!\n\n--- Refinement Cycle 2/5 ---\nCycle 2 score: 2.591965252935756\n\n--- Refinement Cycle 3/5 ---\nCycle 3 score: 2.5919652884375406\n\n--- Refinement Cycle\
    \ 4/5 ---\nCycle 4 score: 2.591965288495362\n\n--- Refinement Cycle 5/5 ---\nCycle 5 score: 2.59196528855486\n\nDE Hybrid strategy complete. Best score: 4.469544971131603\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scipy/optimize/_differentialevolution.py:502: UserWarning: differential evolution didn't find a solution satisfying the constraints, attempting to polish from the least infeasible solution\n  ret = solver.solve()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scipy/optimize/_differentiable_functions.py:376: UserWarning: delta_grad == 0.0. Check if the approximated function is linear. If the function is linear better results can be obtained by defining the Hessian as zero instead of using quasi-Newton approximations.\n  self.H.update(self.x - self.x_prev, self.g - self.g_prev)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage list noesis`\
