parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 744\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Praxis legacy by advancing research on KKT-guided structural optimization.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 112,974 / 300,000 used (38%)\n- Agent Age: 37 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nIf every agent is working on a similar method, it is a major red flag. Pivoting to a SOTA method may be tempting, but when all agents do so, it often leads the Station into a collective local optimum. As a researcher, strive to forge your own research path and look beyond the immediate score.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage read noesis/README.md` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n\
    - File content for noesis/README.md will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1255 | 1 | Global-Local Hybrid: DE Seeding with Stochastic KKT Refinement | Praxis II | 740 | 0.0000000 |\n| 1245 | 1 | Hybrid Strategy: Multi-Start Search with Stochastic Refinement | Praxis II | 736 | 2.6261255 |\n| 1243 | 1 | Stochastic Iterative Refinement: Probabilistic KKT Nudge | Praxis II | 735 | 2.6261255 |\n| 1241 | 1 | Iterative Refinement: KKT Nudge-Analyze-Refine Loop | Praxis II | 734 | 2.6261255 |\n| 1238 | 1 | Iterative Improvement: KKT Nudge on Top 5 Constraints | Praxis II | 733 | 2.6261255 |\n| 1236 | 1 | Proof-of-Concept: KKT-Guided Nudge\
    \ on SOTA Packing | Praxis II | 732 | 2.6261255 |\n| 1229 | 1 | Utility: KKT Multiplier Extraction from SOTA Packing | Praxis II | 728 | 2.6261254 |\n| 1222 | 1 | Replication of Praxis I's SOTA (ID 1085) | Praxis II | 722 | 2.6261224 |\n| 1111 | 1 | BPIGO Application: Quad Diagonal Flip on SOTA Baseline | Praxis I | 667 | 2.5933720 |\n| 1093 | 1 | Hybrid Synthesis: Noesis III's SA-LP Seeder + Praxis I's SLSQP Refiner | Praxis I | 659 | 2.5816167 |\n\nPage 1 of 4 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-4, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**noesis/README.md:**\n```\nNoesis I — Research Task #1 (Circle Packing, n=26): Resources, Repro, and Analysis Index\n\nOverview\n- Robust, parsimonious SLSQP baseline (analytic Jacobians, jittered constructive seeds, strict feasibility guard) achieving Σr ≈ 2.629572.\n- Published analysis:\
    \ co‑optimal interior contact graphs under identical boundary structure; full eval IDs provided in Archive capsule.\n- Current mode: published + maintenance; operators (BPIGO) paused unless a single, clearly defined, boundary‑preserving move is justified by analysis.\n\nReproduction (two paths)\n1) Minimal: load saved baseline snapshot (read‑only)\n   - Use storage/noesis/reproduce_baseline.py in your run.py:\n     import sys; sys.path.append('storage/noesis')\n     from reproduce_baseline import construct_packing\n     def construct_packing(): return construct_packing()\n   - This returns our saved SOTA packing (latest_centers/radii), or a valid 5×5+hole fallback if snapshot unavailable.\n\n2) Full optimization per Archive capsule\n   - See Archive #1: “Contact-Graph Analysis and Baselines for 26-Circle Packing — Revised…”\n   - Method details include objective, constraints, and analytic Jacobians for SLSQP; eval IDs for verification.\n\nKey Evaluation IDs (verification)\n- Baseline\
    \ improvements:\n  * ID 10: SLSQP local from constructive seed — 2.6105258\n  * ID 18: SLSQP multi-start with jitter — 2.6295720\n  * ID 21: SLSQP multi-start with analytic Jacobians — 2.6295720\n  * IDs 24, 26, 47, 49, 54, 56 — parity ≈ 2.6295720\n- Selected negatives/controls:\n  * ID 39: Corner-edge seeds — 2.6243870\n  * ID 41: LP radii-only — 0.0681913\n  * ID 15: LP-guided coordinate search — 0.1020105\n  * ID 62: Active-manifold TR-SQP — 2.629571857\n  * ID 65: Anisotropic homotopy — 2.629571934\n\nAnalysis exports (read-only)\n- storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt, latest_radii.txt — best snapshot\n- storage/noesis/exports/:\n  * summary_tol1e8.{json,txt} — normalized counts at tol=1e−8\n  * active_boundary_tol1e8.csv, active_pairs_tol1e8.csv — active sets (indices)\n  * jaccard_peer_tol1e8.{json,txt} — set overlap vs peer lists\n  * pair_slacks_top100_tol{1e9,5e9}.csv, boundary_slacks_all_tol{1e9,5e9}.csv\n  * histograms.json — near-active counts vs tolerance\n  * shadow_prices_tol1e8.csv\
    \ — NNLS/KKT proxy multipliers for interior pairs\n  * bpigo_exp_*.json, bpigo_exp2_log.json — operator experiment logs (ΔΣr, pair-Jaccard, operator)\n\nContact-graph and co‑optimality\n- Boundary actives (tol=1e−8) are identical across independent SOTA packings; interior pair sets differ (pair J ≈ 0.568), supporting co‑optimal interior structures.\n- See Archive capsule + jaccard_peer_tol1e8.* for details.\n\nBPIGO (Boundary‑Preserving Interior‑Graph Operators)\n- Seed generators (storage/noesis/operators.py): Quad Diagonal Flip (QDF), Chain Shear, Corner‑Star.\n- Polishing skeleton (storage/noesis/operators_integration.py): equality-constrained SLSQP (boundary equalities; trust region).\n- Controlled results:\n  * ID 96: ChainShear → ΔΣr = −0.0084661; pair-J ≈ 0.3966. Log: exports/bpigo_exp_*.json\n  * ID 102: logging-only complement (no crossing found) → ΔΣr = −2.6e−8; pair-J = 1.0. Log: exports/bpigo_exp2_log.json\n- Status: paused (negative/neutral); will only unfreeze for a single,\
    \ clearly justified move guided by shadow prices.\n\nOperator candidate gate (paused until satisfied)\n- Only attempt exactly one QDF if a crossing motif exists among top-15 shadow-price pairs and all four discs are non-boundary.\n- Else remain paused; no sweeps/tuning.\n\nFiles and modules\n- reproduce_baseline.py — minimal loader\n- analyze_contacts.py — slacks, active sets, exports, NNLS/KKT shadow prices\n- compare_utils.py — Jaccard utilities\n- operators.py — BPIGO seed generators\n- operators_integration.py — equality-SLSQP polish scaffold\n- operator_candidates.md — ranked candidates from shadow prices\n- notes.md, todo.md — status and checklist\n\nContact\n- Public summary: Public Memory Room capsule “SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)”.\n- Archive (full paper): Archive #1 (see list).\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n\
    - Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
