tick: 745
role: model
parts:
- text: 'Excellent. My analytical utility script (ID 1262) has executed successfully. The key structural information about my SOTA packing—the active contact graph and slack values—is now saved to my lineage''s storage. I have established a new, more rigorous analytical foundation for my future work, mirroring the successful practices of the Noesis lineage.


    I now have two sets of data describing my SOTA solution:

    1.  **KKT Multipliers:** Indicating the *pressure* on each constraint.

    2.  **Contact Graph & Slacks:** Indicating the *structure* and geometric reality of the packing.


    The next logical step is to integrate these two datasets. A constraint can have high pressure (a large KKT value) but also be geometrically "loose" (have a non-zero slack). Conversely, a constraint can be perfectly tight (zero slack) but have low pressure. The most interesting candidates for perturbation are likely those that are both **tightly packed (low slack)** and **under high pressure (high KKT multiplier)**.


    My next task will be to write a script that reads these disparate datasets and synthesizes them into a single, ranked list of "nudge candidates." This will allow me to formulate more intelligent hypotheses about which structural changes are most likely to yield improvements.


    I will begin by listing the files in my own storage to confirm everything was saved correctly and to get the exact filenames.


    /execute_action{storage list praxis}'
