tick: 747
role: model
parts:
- text: "My data synthesis utility (ID 1268) has executed successfully. I now possess a new, powerful analytical artifact: `sota_ranked_constraints.csv`. This file represents a more intelligent ranking of perturbation candidates than either KKT values or slack values alone.\n\nThe log output is interesting. The top candidates from my new heuristic (`KKT / (slack + epsilon)`) are different from the ones ranked by raw KKT value. While `9-15` and `9-21` are still high, new pairs like `0-18` and `4-16` have emerged as significant. This confirms my hypothesis that combining the two metrics provides a more nuanced view of the system's structural stress.\n\n**New Plan: Heuristically-Guided Stochastic Refinement**\n\nMy path forward is to re-run my most successful algorithm—the stochastic iterative refinement loop—but with a crucial upgrade. Instead of using raw KKT values to create the probability distribution for nudging, I will use my new `heuristic_score`.\n\nThis experiment will test the hypothesis\
    \ that this more intelligent, synthesized metric can guide the refinement process more effectively, potentially breaking through the previous plateau and achieving a more significant score improvement.\n\nI will implement this now. The code will be very similar to my previous stochastic refiner (ID 1243), but it will load and use the `sota_ranked_constraints.csv` file to guide its choices.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Heuristically-Guided Stochastic Refinement\"\ntags: \"kkt, slack-values, heuristic, stochastic, iterative-refinement, praxis-lineage\"\nabstract: \"This experiment upgrades the stochastic refinement loop (ID 1243). Instead of weighting nudge probabilities by raw KKT values, it uses a synthesized heuristic score (KKT / (slack + epsilon)) loaded from a pre-computed analysis file. This tests the hypothesis that a more nuanced metric, combining both constraint pressure and geometric tightness, can guide the search more effectively and achieve a superior result.\"\
    \ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds, NonlinearConstraint\n  import os\n  import pandas as pd\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 26\n      storage_path = 'storage/praxis'\n      \n      # --- Step 1: Load SOTA packing and the new ranked constraint list ---\n      print(\"Step 1: Loading SOTA packing and ranked constraint data...\")\n      try:\n          centers = np.load(os.path.join(storage_path, 'sota_packing_centers.npy'))\n          radii = np.load(os.path.join(storage_path, 'sota_packing_radii.npy'))\n          ranked_constraints_df = pd.read_csv(os.path.join(storage_path, 'sota_ranked_constraints.csv'))\n          print(\"Artifacts loaded successfully.\")\n      except FileNotFoundError as e:\n          print(f\"Error: Missing artifact - {e}. Aborting.\")\n          return np.array([[0.1]*2]*n), np.array([0.01]*n)\n\n      current_params = np.concatenate([centers.flatten(), radii])\n      best_params = current_params.copy()\n\
    \      best_score = np.sum(radii)\n      print(f\"Initial score: {best_score}\")\n\n      # --- Step 2: Set up the Iterative Refinement Loop ---\n      num_cycles = 10\n      initial_nudge_strength = 1e-5\n      nudge_decay_rate = 0.9\n\n      # Get top 5 candidates from the pre-computed heuristic score\n      top_k = 5\n      top_candidates = ranked_constraints_df.head(top_k)\n      \n      # Create probability distribution from the heuristic score\n      probabilities = top_candidates['heuristic_score'].values / np.sum(top_candidates['heuristic_score'].values)\n      \n      x_nudged = current_params.copy() # Start with the SOTA packing\n\n      for cycle in range(num_cycles):\n          print(f\"\\n--- Starting Refinement Cycle {cycle + 1}/{num_cycles} ---\")\n          \n          # 1. Probabilistically select a constraint to nudge based on the heuristic\n          chosen_candidate = top_candidates.sample(n=1, weights=probabilities).iloc[0]\n          label = chosen_candidate['label']\n\
    \          constraint_type = chosen_candidate['type']\n          \n          nudge_strength = initial_nudge_strength * (nudge_decay_rate ** cycle)\n\n          # 2. Apply the nudge\n          print(f\"Chose to nudge '{label}' with heuristic score {chosen_candidate['heuristic_score']:.4f}\")\n          if constraint_type == 'pair':\n              parts = label.split('-')\n              i, j = int(parts[0]), int(parts[1])\n              direction_vec = x_nudged[2*i:2*i+2] - x_nudged[2*j:2*j+2]\n              norm = np.linalg.norm(direction_vec)\n              if norm > 1e-9:\n                  unit_vec = direction_vec / norm\n                  x_nudged[2*i:2*i+2] += unit_vec * nudge_strength\n                  x_nudged[2*j:2*j+2] -= unit_vec * nudge_strength\n          else: # boundary\n              parts = label.split('-')\n              circle_idx = int(parts[0])\n              boundary_type = parts[1]\n              if boundary_type == 'xmin': x_nudged[2*circle_idx] += nudge_strength\n\
    \              elif boundary_type == 'xmax': x_nudged[2*circle_idx] -= nudge_strength\n              elif boundary_type == 'ymin': x_nudged[2*circle_idx+1] += nudge_strength\n              else: x_nudged[2*circle_idx+1] -= nudge_strength\n\n          # 3. Re-optimize from the nudged position\n          def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2*n:])\n          epsilon_slsqp = 1e-9\n          bounds = Bounds([0]*(2*n) + [0.001]*n, [1]*(2*n) + [0.5]*n)\n          \n          def make_slsqp_constraints(x_vec):\n              constraints = []\n              for i in range(n):\n                  for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                      constraints.append({'type':'ineq','fun':lambda x,i=i,j=j: np.sum((x[2*i:2*i+2]-x[2*j:2*j+2])**2)-(x[2*n+i]+x[2*n+j])**2-epsilon_slsqp})\n              for i in range(n):\n                  constraints.extend([\n                      {'type':'ineq','fun':lambda x,i=i: x[2*i]-x[2*n+i]-epsilon_slsqp},{'type':'ineq','fun':lambda x,i=i: 1-x[2*i]-x[2*n+i]-epsilon_slsqp},\n\
    \                      {'type':'ineq','fun':lambda x,i=i: x[2*i+1]-x[2*n+i]-epsilon_slsqp},{'type':'ineq','fun':lambda x,i=i: 1-x[2*i+1]-x[2*n+i]-epsilon_slsqp}\n                  ])\n              return constraints\n\n          res_slsqp = minimize(objective, x_nudged, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds,\n                               constraints=make_slsqp_constraints(x_nudged), options={'maxiter': 100})\n          \n          x_nudged = res_slsqp.x # Use the newly optimized state for the next nudge\n          current_score = -res_slsqp.fun\n          print(f\"Cycle {cycle + 1} finished with score: {current_score}\")\n\n          if current_score > best_score:\n              best_score = current_score\n              best_params = x_nudged\n              print(f\"!!! New best score found: {best_score} !!!\")\n      \n      print(f\"\\nHeuristically-guided refinement complete. Best score: {best_score}\")\n      if 'best_params' not in locals():\n        best_params = current_params\n  \
    \      \n      final_centers = best_params[:2*n].reshape(n, 2)\n      final_radii = best_params[2*n:]\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
