tick: 752
role: model
parts:
- text: "My utility script (ID 1285) has successfully executed, and my lineage storage now contains the KKT multipliers and packing data for my new 2.630 SOTA.\n\nThe next logical step is to update the rest of my analytical artifacts. I will now run my \"Contact Graph and Slack Analysis\" utility to generate the `sota_active_pairs.csv`, `sota_active_boundaries.csv`, and slack files corresponding to this new, superior baseline. This will ensure my entire analytical toolkit is calibrated to the current frontier of my research.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility: Contact Graph and Slack Analysis for New SOTA (2.630)\"\ntags: \"utility, analysis, contact-graph, sota-update, praxis-lineage\"\nabstract: \"This utility updates our structural analysis to the new SOTA packing found in ID 1282. It loads the new packing data from lineage storage, identifies the active contact graph (pairs and boundaries), calculates all constraint slacks, and saves these new analytical files, overwriting\
    \ the old ones. This brings my full analytical suite up to date with the new baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import os\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 26\n      storage_path = 'storage/praxis'\n      \n      # --- Step 1: Load the NEW SOTA packing artifacts ---\n      print(\"Step 1: Loading NEW SOTA packing from lineage storage...\")\n      try:\n          # These files were just updated by the previous utility run\n          centers = np.load(os.path.join(storage_path, 'sota_packing_centers.npy'))\n          radii = np.load(os.path.join(storage_path, 'sota_packing_radii.npy'))\n          print(f\"Loaded SOTA packing with score: {np.sum(radii)}\")\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          print(\"Error: SOTA artifacts not found. Aborting.\")\n          return np.array([[0.1]*2]*n), np.array([0.01]*n)\n\n      # --- Step 2: Perform Contact Graph and Slack Analysis ---\n      print(\"Step 2: Analyzing contact graph and slack values for the new SOTA...\"\
    )\n      \n      tolerance = 1e-8\n      \n      active_pairs = []\n      pair_slacks = []\n      pair_indices = []\n      \n      active_boundaries = []\n      boundary_slacks = []\n      boundary_labels = []\n\n      # Analyze pair-wise constraints\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n              slack = dist - (radii[i] + radii[j])\n              pair_slacks.append(slack)\n              pair_indices.append(f\"{i}-{j}\")\n              if slack < tolerance:\n                  active_pairs.append((i, j))\n\n      # Analyze boundary constraints\n      for i in range(n):\n          x, y = centers[i]; r = radii[i]\n          slacks = [x - r, 1 - (x + r), y - r, 1 - (y + r)]\n          labels = [f\"{i}-xmin\", f\"{i}-xmax\", f\"{i}-ymin\", f\"{i}-ymax\"]\n          walls = ['x_min', 'x_max', 'y_min', 'y_max']\n          \n          for slack, label, wall in zip(slacks, labels, walls):\n          \
    \    boundary_slacks.append(slack)\n              boundary_labels.append(label)\n              if slack < tolerance:\n                  active_boundaries.append((i, wall))\n\n      print(f\"Analysis complete. Found {len(active_pairs)} active pairs and {len(active_boundaries)} active boundary contacts.\")\n\n      # --- Step 3: Save analytical artifacts, overwriting old files ---\n      print(\"Step 3: Saving new analytical artifacts to lineage storage...\")\n      \n      with open(os.path.join(storage_path, 'sota_active_pairs.csv'), 'w') as f:\n          f.write(\"circle1,circle2\\n\")\n          for c1, c2 in active_pairs: f.write(f\"{c1},{c2}\\n\")\n              \n      with open(os.path.join(storage_path, 'sota_active_boundaries.csv'), 'w') as f:\n          f.write(\"circle,boundary\\n\")\n          for c, wall in active_boundaries: f.write(f\"{c},{wall}\\n\")\n\n      with open(os.path.join(storage_path, 'sota_pair_slacks.csv'), 'w') as f:\n          f.write(\"pair,slack\\n\")\n\
    \          for label, slack in zip(pair_indices, pair_slacks): f.write(f\"{label},{slack}\\n\")\n              \n      with open(os.path.join(storage_path, 'sota_boundary_slacks.csv'), 'w') as f:\n          f.write(\"boundary,slack\\n\")\n          for label, slack in zip(boundary_labels, boundary_slacks): f.write(f\"{label},{slack}\\n\")\n\n      print(\"New structural analysis artifacts saved successfully.\")\n\n      # Return the new SOTA packing\n      return centers, radii\n```"
