tick: 755
role: model
parts:
- text: "My reflection is complete. I have a clear plan for both the immediate technical challenge and my actions upon reaching maturity. My next experiment will adapt my proven KKT-guided refinement loop to optimize the boundary constraints of my new \"rattler\" SOTA.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter and implement this new experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Boundary-Focused KKT Refinement for Rattler SOTA\"\ntags: \"kkt, boundary-optimization, rattler, iterative-refinement, praxis-lineage\"\nabstract: \"My new SOTA (ID 1282) is a 'rattler' configuration with no internal contacts, making previous refinement methods obsolete. This experiment adapts the stochastic KKT-guided loop to this new paradigm. It exclusively analyzes, ranks, and nudges the boundary constraints, where all the structural pressure now lies. This tests if the refinement methodology can be successfully applied to this different class of optimum.\"\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds, NonlinearConstraint\n  import os\n  import pandas as pd\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 26\n      storage_path = 'storage/praxis'\n      \n      print(\"Step 1: Loading new SOTA packing and its KKT data...\")\n      try:\n          centers = np.load(os.path.join(storage_path, 'sota_packing_centers.npy'))\n          radii = np.load(os.path.join(storage_path, 'sota_packing_radii.npy'))\n          kkt_multipliers = np.load(os.path.join(storage_path, 'sota_kkt_multipliers.npy'))\n      except FileNotFoundError as e:\n          print(f\"Error: Missing artifact - {e}. Aborting.\")\n          return np.array([[0.1]*2]*n), np.array([0.01]*n)\n\n      current_params = np.concatenate([centers.flatten(), radii])\n      best_params = current_params.copy()\n      best_score = np.sum(radii)\n      print(f\"Initial score: {best_score}\")\n\n      num_cycles = 10\n      initial_nudge_strength = 1e-6 # Using a\
    \ smaller nudge for boundary tuning\n      nudge_decay_rate = 0.95\n\n      # --- Setup for SLSQP and KKT Analysis ---\n      def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2*n:])\n      epsilon = 1e-9\n      bounds = Bounds([0]*(2*n) + [0.001]*n, [1]*(2*n) + [0.5]*n)\n      \n      def make_slsqp_constraints(x_vec):\n          constraints = []\n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i+1,n): constraints.append({'type':'ineq','fun':lambda x,i=i,j=j:np.sum((x[2*i:2*i+2]-x[2*j:2*j+2])**2)-(x[2*n+i]+x[2*n+j])**2-epsilon})\n              constraints.extend([{'type':'ineq','fun':lambda x,i=i:x[2*i]-x[2*n+i]-epsilon},{'type':'ineq','fun':lambda x,i=i:1-x[2*i]-x[2*n+i]-epsilon},{'type':'ineq','fun':lambda x,i=i:x[2*i+1]-x[2*n+i]-epsilon},{'type':'ineq','fun':lambda x,i=i:1-x[2*i+1]-x[2*n+i]-epsilon}])\n          return constraints\n\n      # --- Iterative Refinement Loop (Boundary-Focused) ---\n      for cycle in range(num_cycles):\n          print(f\"\\n--- Starting Boundary Refinement\
    \ Cycle {cycle + 1}/{num_cycles} ---\")\n          \n          # 1. Get KKT multipliers for the CURRENT packing\n          # (We must re-analyze each cycle as the pressures change)\n          def constraints_fun(x):\n              non_overlap=[np.sum((x[2*i:2*i+2]-x[2*j:2*j+2])**2)-(x[2*n+i]+x[2*n+j])**2 for i in range(n) for j in range(i+1,n)]\n              b_c=[c for i in range(n) for c in [x[2*i]-x[2*n+i],1-x[2*i]-x[2*n+i],x[2*i+1]-x[2*n+i],1-x[2*i+1]-x[2*n+i]]]\n              return np.concatenate([np.array(non_overlap), np.array(b_c)])\n          num_non_overlap = n*(n-1)//2\n          nlc = NonlinearConstraint(constraints_fun, np.zeros(num_non_overlap+4*n), np.inf)\n          res_kkt = minimize(objective, current_params, method='trust-constr', bounds=bounds, constraints=[nlc], options={'maxiter': 1})\n          kkt_multipliers = res_kkt.v[0]\n          \n          # 2. Isolate, rank, and probabilistically select a BOUNDARY constraint\n          boundary_kkt_start_index = num_non_overlap\n\
    \          boundary_kkt_values = kkt_multipliers[boundary_kkt_start_index:]\n          \n          top_k = 5\n          # Get indices relative to the start of the boundary multipliers array\n          relative_top_k_indices = np.argsort(boundary_kkt_values)[-top_k:][::-1]\n          top_k_values = boundary_kkt_values[relative_top_k_indices]\n          \n          if np.sum(top_k_values) < 1e-9:\n              print(\"Boundary KKT values are negligible. Halting refinement.\")\n              break\n\n          probabilities = top_k_values / np.sum(top_k_values)\n          chosen_relative_index = np.random.choice(relative_top_k_indices, p=probabilities)\n          \n          x_nudged = res_kkt.x.copy()\n          nudge_strength = initial_nudge_strength * (nudge_decay_rate ** cycle)\n\n          # 3. Apply the nudge\n          circle_idx = chosen_relative_index % n\n          boundary_type = chosen_relative_index // n # 0:xmin, 1:xmax, 2:ymin, 3:ymax\n          \n          print(f\"Chose\
    \ to nudge boundary constraint for circle {circle_idx} (type {boundary_type})\")\n          if boundary_type == 0: x_nudged[2*circle_idx] += nudge_strength\n          elif boundary_type == 1: x_nudged[2*circle_idx] -= nudge_strength\n          elif boundary_type == 2: x_nudged[2*circle_idx+1] += nudge_strength\n          else: x_nudged[2*circle_idx+1] -= nudge_strength\n\n          # 4. Re-optimize\n          res_slsqp = minimize(objective, x_nudged, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds,\n                               constraints=make_slsqp_constraints(x_nudged), options={'maxiter': 100})\n          \n          current_params = res_slsqp.x\n          current_score = -res_slsqp.fun\n          print(f\"Cycle {cycle + 1} finished with score: {current_score}\")\n\n          if current_score > best_score:\n              best_score = current_score\n              best_params = current_params\n              print(f\"!!! New best score found: {best_score} !!!\")\n\n      print(f\"\\nBoundary refinement\
    \ complete. Best score: {best_score}\")\n      final_centers = best_params[:2*n].reshape(n, 2)\n      final_radii = best_params[2*n:]\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
