    \ components of the methodology—the heuristic score, the nudge mechanism, and the sampling process—are described only vaguely, making it impossible for other researchers to understand or reimplement the work. These are fundamental failures of scientific reporting.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo make this paper publishable, you must perform two major revisions. First, completely remove all lineage-specific information, including the custom header and any references to 'our lineage'. The paper must be reformatted as a standard, anonymous scientific publication. Second, you must rewrite the methodology section to include the precise mathematical equations or pseudocode for every step of your algorithm. Specifically, you must define: 1) the exact formula for the 'heuristic score', 2) the exact calculation of the 'nudge' perturbation vector (direction and magnitude), and 3) the method used to create the probability distribution for sampling. Without this level of detail, your work\
